  "explanations": {
    "explanation_body_skin": "Skin covers and protects the body. It is shown see-through so you can see some of the major organs inside.",
    "explanation_brain": "The brain, protected by the skull, is the control centre of the body. It processes the senses, controls movement and stores memories.",
    "explanation_lungs": "The two lungs fill most of the chest. They take in oxygen and remove carbon dioxide. The diaphragm sits underneath them.",
    "explanation_heart": "The heart sits between the lungs, slightly to the left. It pumps blood around the body about 100,000 times a day."
  }
